1d72d9c7 [@] currently focused on accepting and interacting with bots on port 8081
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #Looking at the code, the bot interaction on port 8081 is handled by the `slopprompt.ts` module
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #(exported functions: `listenService`, `slopBroadcast`, `announceCommand`) and consumed in
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #`relay.ts` via `slopPrompt` which races between stdin reads and network connections.
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #Current Architecture
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #1. `listenService()` (in `slopprompt.ts`):
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #   - Starts a TCP listener on `localhost:8081` (configurable in `relay.ts` via `listen` config
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #flag).
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #   - Calls `acceptConnections()`, which loops `listener.accept()` and for each new connection:
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #     - Stores it in `slopConnections` (Map).
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #     - Starts a `readNamedConnection` promise (reads from the socket asynchronously).
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #     - Stores the promise in `receivePromises` (object).
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #2. `slopPrompt()` (in `slopprompt.ts`):
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #   - The main prompt loop races:
1d72db09 [deepseek-v4] #     - `readPromise` — a pending `reader.read()` from stdin.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #     - `timerPromise` — a 20ms timeout (interval parameter).
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #     - `listenerPromise` (optional) — if listener is active.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #     - All `receivePromises` values (TCP read promises).
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #   - When a TCP read promise resolves, it parses the JSON (expects `{messages: [{message, from}]}`
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #or `{command: {name, args, from}}`) and stores the result in `response.messages` or
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #`response.line`.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #   - That response is then returned to `chat()` loop in `relay.ts`, where messages are pushed to
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #`rohaHistory` and optionally commands are executed.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #3. `slopBroadcast()` (in `slopprompt.ts`):
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #   - Writes NDJSON to all connected sockets. Currently iterates over `slopConnections`, writes JSON
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #like `{"messages":[{"message":"...","from":"..."}]}\n`.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #   - Handles partial writes by looping.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #Potential Issues & Observations
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #- Single-connection handling – `receivePromises` is an object (not Map) keyed by connection
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #name. When a read promise resolves, it’s deleted and a new one is started. That’s correct, but the
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #`readNamedConnection` function `setNoDelay` is not called.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #- No connection heartbeats – If a bot disconnects ungracefully, the read promise may hang
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #indefinitely (until a timeout on the socket). The code in `slopBroadcast` removes connections that
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #cause write errors, but there’s no proactive cleanup for dead reads.
1d72db0a [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #- JSON parsing fragility – `slopPrompt` parses the entire buffer as a single JSON object.
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #If the bot sends multiple JSON objects concatenated (NDJSON), only the first is parsed; the rest is
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #lost. The current design assumes exactly one JSON per read. Better to use a line-based (or
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #newline-delimited) parser.
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #- No queue for incoming messages – The race model means one bot message is processed per
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #iteration of the prompt loop. If a bot sends many messages quickly, they might be interleaved or
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #starved.
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #- Error handling – `acceptConnections` runs an infinite loop but if `listener.accept()`
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #throws (e.g., too many open files), the loop exits and no further connections are accepted. The
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #listener promise in the race will also reject.
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #- Security – No authentication; any local process can connect to port 8081.
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #Suggestions for Improvement
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #1. Wrap sockets with a line-based reader – Use a `BufferedReader` (e.g., `Deno.BufReader`)
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #or implement a simple splitter that buffers partial reads and emits complete lines.
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #2. Add connection health tracking – Use a timeout for read promises (e.g., `Promise.race`
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #with a timeout). If a socket hasn’t sent data in N seconds, close it and remove from
1d72db0b [deepseek-v4] #`receivePromises`.
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #3. Queue incoming messages – Instead of returning to the prompt loop one at a time,
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #accumulate messages from all races and batch process them. Or at least use an array for pending
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #messages.
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #4. Resilient acceptor loop – Catch errors in `acceptConnections` and re-enter the loop
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #(with a brief delay) to keep the port open.
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #5. Clearer protocol – Document that the expected format is NDJSON with `{messages: [...]}`
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #or `{command: {...}}`. Ensure both sides agree.
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #6. Optional authentication – Add a simple token handshake on connect (e.g., first message
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #includes an API key) for production use.
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #Would you like me to provide example code for any of these improvements, or do you have a specific
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #issue you're encountering with bot interaction?
1d72db0c [deepseek-v4] #
