1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #The shared files appear to be the core of a research tool called Slop Relay — a
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #multi-model, multi-user chat relay that interfaces with various LLM providers (OpenAI, DeepSeek,
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #Google, Anthropic) alongside a custom raw‑mode prompt handler and a Discord bot interface.
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #Key observations:
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #- Structure – The system uses a packed, tab‑indented TypeScript style. Named functions are
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #used extensively, which aligns with the stated preference.
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #- Async architecture – `Promise.race` drives the main prompt loop, interleaving stdin,
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #connection accepts, and bot messages. This is a clean pattern for a single‑threaded event loop.
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #- Unicode handling – Custom width calculations (`stringWidth`, `discordStringWidth`) and
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #grapheme segmentation for raw terminal input. Robust for emoji and wide characters.
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #- Shortcode expansion – Live replacement of `:shortcode:` sequences, useful for chat
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #environments.
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #- Tool integration – Models can call functions (`readtime`, `submitfile`,
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #`fetchfile`, `tagslop`) with recursive relay depth.
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #- Connection management – Accepts remote bot connections on port 8081, sends
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #NDJSON‑formatted messages.
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #Potential areas for refinement (if you’re open to suggestions):
1dae6a37 [deepseek-v4] #
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #1. Type safety – Several `any` and implicit `unknown` types (e.g., `grokThink`,
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #`roha.config`). Stronger typing would reduce runtime surprises.
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #2. Error handling – The `callCommand` switch has a blanket `try/catch`; individual branches
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #could benefit from more granular recovery.
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #3. Memory – `rohaHistory` grows unbounded; a configurable sliding window or summarisation
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #might be needed for long sessions.
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #4. Connection resilience – Remote connections are dropped with `faking it until we make it`
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #messages; a structured reconnection strategy could improve reliability.
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #If you’d like deeper analysis of a specific module or have questions about the design, feel free to
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #ask.
1dae6a38 [deepseek-v4] #
