1dae92aa [deepseek-v4] #   but in `main()` the chroma state machine is on `pio1`. This will cause the DMA to never trigger
1dae92aa [deepseek-v4] #or to read from the wrong FIFO. It should be `piogetdreq(pio, sm, true)` using the passed
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #`PIO` parameter.
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #2. FDEBUG stall checks for chroma on pio0
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #   The code checks `pio0->fdebug` for `chromaStall`, but the chroma state machine is on `pio1`.
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #This will never flag a stall. A similar oversight exists for teletext (which is correctly on pio0).
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #3. Chroma DMA transfer count
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #   The chroma PIO uses `FIFOJOINTX` and expects `colorWords` (120) words per field. That
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #matches your pre‑computed tables (120 entries). However, each word represents 2 subcarrier cycles,
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #so 120 words = 240 subcarrier cycles = ~13.5 µs. Is that enough for the active line? PAL active
1dae92ab [deepseek-v4] #line is ~52 µs, so you may need more words or a different loop in the PIO. The `chroma.pio` loop
