1db0f103 [deepseek-v4] #DMA only at the start of a new field, e.g., by waiting for the vsync IRQ or using DMA chaining. The
1db0f103 [deepseek-v4] #current approach may work because the DMA transfer length is exactly the number of words needed for
1db0f103 [deepseek-v4] #one field, but any timing variation could cause glitches.
1db0f103 [deepseek-v4] #
1db0f103 [deepseek-v4] #What is new or different
1db0f104 [deepseek-v4] #- Combined mono video + colour subcarrier + teletext on RP2350 – most examples focus on one
1db0f104 [deepseek-v4] #feature. The integration of all three via separate PIO state machines is novel.
