1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #Suggestions for Improvement
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #1. Fix PIO pin direction usage: Replace `set pindirs, 0/1` with `set pins, 0/1` and keep
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #the pin always output. Keep `out pindirs, 1` only if you really intend to toggle direction
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #(unlikely). Use `out pins, 1` for active video.
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #2. Correct chroma clock divider: Change `piosmset_clkdiv(pio,sm,2.3471f)` to
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #`9.3885f` (or compute more precisely: 166.5 / (4*4.43361875) ≈ 9.3885). Also ensure the chroma PIO
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #waits for IRQ from video; either enable IRQ 4 in `vidbit.pio` or use a different sync method.
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #3. Initialize ISR for pixel count: In `vidbit.pio`, before the line loop, load the pixel
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #counter into ISR: `mov isr, y` or `out isr, 32` after loading y from FIFO. Currently it’s using
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #`mov y, isr` without initializing ISR. That will give undefined behavior.
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #4. Document timing: Add a comment block in `vidbit.pio` that calculates each segment:
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #HSYNC, back porch, active, front porch, and sum to 10656 cycles. Verify with actual numbers.
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #5. Modularize frame buffer allocation: Move declarations of `evenFrame`, `oddFrame`,
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #`evenWords`, `oddWords` into a shared header (e.g., `pal576i.h`). Use `constexpr` or `#define` for
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #line counts.
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #6. Pre‑compute teletext packets: Instead of recomputing each field, build a static teletext
1e051350 [deepseek-v4] #page and only update when needed (e.g., on text input). The current per‑field rebuild is fine for a
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #demo, but might lag if the CPU is busy.
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #7. Consider using PIO’s `irq` for field sync: Set an IRQ flag in the video PIO at the end
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #of each field (or line) to trigger the chroma PIO to start. The chroma PIO could use `wait 1 irq 4`
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #and then process the next field’s chroma data. This would eliminate the need for the main loop to
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #poll.
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #8. Double‑buffer for chroma: The chroma DMA is set to a ring buffer; if you want
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #alternating even/odd fields, you could have two separate buffers and switch DMA reads per field,
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #similar to video.
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #9. Remove unused code: e.g., `static uint32_t pcm32=0;` not used, `int pioStatus` assigned
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #but never checked, `bool led` global.
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #10. Add error handling: e.g., `piocanadd_program` returns false, but code only does
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #`pass&=...` and continues. Print a diagnostic or halt.
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #Conclusion
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #This is a sophisticated project that shows excellent use of PIO and DMA on the RP2350. The main
1e051351 [deepseek-v4] #issues are the pin direction confusion in `vidbit.pio` and the chroma clock divider. With those
1e051352 [deepseek-v4] #fixed, the conceptual design is sound. The interlace, teletext, and chroma overlays are nice
1e051352 [deepseek-v4] #features. I encourage you to keep refining and document the timing constraints.
1e051352 [deepseek-v4] #
1e051352 [deepseek-v4] #If you have specific questions about any part, feel free to ask. I’m happy to help debug or suggest
1e051352 [deepseek-v4] #alternative implementations.
1e051352 [deepseek-v4] #
