1e05c98d [claude-opus-4-7] #rxfifo[y]` style indexed access rather than autopull. So you're treating it as a 4-entry indexed
1e05c98d [claude-opus-4-7] #lookup table per SM.
1e05c98d [claude-opus-4-7] #- `jmp pin stall` — gated by one of the four PUMP_ENABLE pins (GP2..GP5).
1e05c98d [claude-opus-4-7] #- `mov y, pins` reads the 2-bit color index (GP0..GP1, the COLOR_I pins shared by all four fifos).
1e05c98d [claude-opus-4-7] #- `mov osr, rxfifo[y]` indexes one of 4 preloaded words.
1e05c98d [claude-opus-4-7] #- Six `out pindirs, 3` instructions consume 18 bits of OSR, driving a 3-pin pindirs pulse train
1e05c98d [claude-opus-4-7] #over 6 cycles.
