1e06cf6c [gemini-3.1-pro] #However, we need to take a close look at the `colorpump.pio` file. There is a sneaky logical bug in
1e06cf6c [gemini-3.1-pro] #how `jmp x--` works, and the cycle-balancing needs to be extremely precise to guarantee exactly 10
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #cycles per pixel across all 4 colors.
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #The `jmp x--` Bug
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #In PIO, `jmp x--, label` means: "If X is not 0, jump to the label. In either case, decrement
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #X."
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #If you cascade them like this:
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #    jmp x--, t3
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #    jmp x--, t2
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #If X is `0`, the first instruction evaluates `0 != 0` (False), so it does not jump, but it
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #still decrements X to `0xFFFFFFFF`. The second instruction then evaluates `0xFFFFFFFF != 0` (True),
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #and jumps to `t2`! This breaks the switch statement entirely.
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #The 10-Cycle Balanced Solution
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #To decode 2 bits in PIO, we have to use a combination of `jmp !x` and `jmp x--`. Because this
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #decoding takes a variable number of cycles depending on the value of X (X=3 takes longer to decode
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #than X=0), we must balance the paths using `nop` delays and inline the end of the loop so every
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #single path takes exactly 10 cycles.
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6d [gemini-3.1-pro] #Here is the corrected and perfectly balanced `colorpump.pio`:
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #; colorpump.pio
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #; outs 2 gpio pins for color index
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #; pulses low 1 of 4 side set pins to trigger a colorfifo
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #; waits for IRQ 0 to start the line, draws fixed pixels, then waits again
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #.program colorpump
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #.wrap_target
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #	wait	1 irq 0 clear
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #	mov	y, isr
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #pixel:
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #	out	pins, 2        ; [1] Shift 2 bits to COLOR_I0,1
1e06cf6e [gemini-3.1-pro] #	out	x, 2           ; [1] Shift 2 bits to X (Pump Select)
