1e426b21 [deepseek-v4] #colorfifo` chain for component YPbPr color are well thought out.
1e426b21 [deepseek-v4] #- The use of DMA to feed PIO FIFOs from pre‑computed frame buffers is standard but effective.
1e426b21 [deepseek-v4] #
1e426b21 [deepseek-v4] #New or Different Elements
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #1. Colour generation via resistor networks – your `colorfifo` and `colorpump` approach uses
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #a bank of 4 PIO state machines on PIO2, each loaded with a 6‑cycle pulse‑train per colour, selected
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #by 2‑bit index pins. This is a creative way to avoid high‑speed DACs while maintaining 6‑bit (or
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #3‑bit per channel) colour depth.
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #2. Teletext with Hamming 8/4 encoding – The WST implementation appears complete, with
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #pre‑computed encoded packets. The interleaving of teletext data on lines 7‑22 is correct for PAL.
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #The inclusion of a rolling row counter (1‑25) is a nice touch for testing.
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #3. Chroma generation – using two pins with resistor weighting (100Ω and 330Ω) and a PIO
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #generating a 4‑phase sine wave for colour burst is a known technique, but the DMA ring buffer to
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #produce a continuous carrier is well executed.
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #4. CDU (CDC) input handling – Using a spin lock and a callback to collect complete lines is
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #robust for a real-time video system.
1e426b22 [deepseek-v4] #
