1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] # ꔀ nitrologic Relay 1.8.7 ⛲  claude-opus-4-8 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.762 344.0KB 34.75s
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #Quite a bundle. The VIDBIT video generator is the heart of it and it's a lovely bit of work —
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #squeezing PAL 576i and 288p out of PIO state machines with resistor-ladder DACs. A few things stood
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #out as new to me:
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #The `vidbit.pio` timing comments are doing the heavy lifting. The sync structure encoded as FIFO
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #words — `[0]` vsync edge count, then `[1..n]` pulse widths, then linecounter and pixelcounter — is
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #a neat way to push the entire field timing through DMA without CPU intervention. The `irq next set
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #6` / `clear 6` bracketing the active region is presumably how you'd hand off to an active-line
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #pumper on the next PIO block.
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #The 2-bits-per-pixel move in `monobit.h` (`bitsPerPixel=2`, `lineWords=27*2`) with the `ditherMem`
1f92fd9c [claude-opus-4-8] #ordered-dither patterns is a clean way to get apparent greys out of a fundamentally binary signal.
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #The `flipBits16` expansion doubling each bit is tidy.
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #The colour path is the most experimental-looking corner — `make_color_train` packing Y/Pb/Pr PDM
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #into a 3-lane bit train, fed through `colorpump` → `colorfifo` on pio2. That
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #`0b0'000'...'111'110'011'001'111` binary grouping in the test trains is very readable.
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #One thing I noticed: `vidbit.md` flags "864 pixels is too many pixels" under INVESTIGATE,
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #and the `mode` string in `vidbit2350.cpp` now says `<VIDBIT MICROPAL 77>`. Is the micropal
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #direction about dropping the active pixel count to ease the PIO/DMA bandwidth?
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #What are you turning your attention to right now — the colour generation, or the pixel-count
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #question?
1f92fd9d [claude-opus-4-8] #
